        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "context",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 870,
            "text": "My use case: To save email resume properly, i need immutable id to reference original email of the resume. This allow me to build a system where every single new email is resume like : “X person ask X person if there is a possibility to do X in comparaison of original X” This remove more than 80% of useless token and simply the context for smaller llm to understand a long email conversation with many ping pong and person inside. I use it to create draft prefill with the good knowledge + compact history of the conversation with each mail resume Any resources to support this? Are you willing to work on this? It’s already done, check out here and feel free to ask me ANYTHING that could increase the speed for a merge, i think this feature is very light but very important when you realise how microsoft manage by default id that can change for no technical reason…",
            "sha256": "8dacf19c1d5cb329f7109a5feaa5780798c58dd27786e3650139d594562b4b29"
          }
